1. User Registration Testing
Test Case 1: Successful User Registration
Steps:
Open the Intercity Ride Sharing System.
Click the Register button.
Enter a valid full name.
Enter a valid email address.
Enter a strong password.
Select a role (Driver or Passenger).
Click Submit.
Expected Result:
The account is created successfully.
The user is redirected to the dashboard.
A success message is displayed.
Test Case 2: Registration with Invalid Email
Steps:
Open the registration form.
Enter an invalid email format.
Fill in the remaining required fields.
Click Submit.
Expected Result:
The system displays an email validation error.
Registration is not completed.
2. Login and Logout Testing
Test Case 1: Successful Login
Steps:
Open the login page.
Enter valid email and password.
Click Login.
Expected Result:
User successfully logs into the system.
Dashboard page opens.
Test Case 2: Invalid Login
Steps:
Open the login page.
Enter incorrect password.
Click Login.
Expected Result:
Error message appears.
User remains on login page.
Test Case 3: Logout
Steps:
Login to the system.
Click Logout.
Expected Result:
User session ends successfully.
Login page is displayed.
3. Driver Feature Testing
Test Case 1: Post New Trip
Steps:
Login as Driver.
Navigate to Post Trip section.
Enter trip details:
Departure location
Destination
Date and time
Available seats
Price
Click Submit.
Expected Result:
Trip is posted successfully.
Trip appears in available trips list.
Test Case 2: Edit Trip
Steps:
Login as Driver.
Open posted trips.
Select Edit.
Modify trip details.
Save changes.
Expected Result:
Updated trip information is saved.
Test Case 3: Delete Trip
Steps:
Login as Driver.
Open trip management page.
Select Delete Trip.
Confirm deletion.
Expected Result:
Trip is removed from the system.
4. Passenger Feature Testing
Test Case 1: Search for Trips
Steps:
Login as Passenger.
Open search page.
Enter departure and destination.
Click Search.
Expected Result:
Matching trips are displayed.
Test Case 2: Filter Trips
Steps:
Search for trips.
Apply filters by:
Price
Time
Location
Expected Result:
Filtered trip results appear correctly.
Test Case 3: View Trip Details
Steps:
Select a trip from search results.
Open trip details page.
Expected Result:
Full trip information is displayed.
5. Booking System Testing
Test Case 1: Successful Seat Booking
Steps:
Login as Passenger.
Select an available trip.
Click Book Seat.
Confirm booking.
Expected Result:
Booking is completed successfully.
Seat count decreases.
Booking confirmation appears.
Test Case 2: Booking with No Available Seats
Steps:
Select a fully booked trip.
Attempt to book a seat.
Expected Result:
System prevents booking.
Error message appears.
6. Payment System Testing
Test Case 1: Successful Payment
Steps:
Select a trip.
Proceed to payment.
Enter valid payment information.
Confirm payment.
Expected Result:
Payment is processed successfully.
Booking confirmation is generated.
Test Case 2: Failed Payment
Steps:
Proceed to payment.
Enter invalid payment details.
Confirm payment.
Expected Result:
Payment fails.
Error message appears.
Booking is not confirmed.
7. Rating and Review Testing
Test Case 1: Passenger Rates Driver
Steps:
Complete a trip.
Open rating section.
Select rating score.
Write review.
Submit review.
Expected Result:
Rating and review are saved successfully.
Test Case 2: Duplicate Review Prevention
Steps:
Submit a review for a completed trip.
Attempt to submit another review for the same trip.
Expected Result:
System blocks duplicate review submission.
8. Security Testing
Test Case 1: SQL Injection Prevention
Steps:
Open login form.
Enter SQL injection code in input fields.
Submit login request.
Expected Result:
Login fails.
System remains secure.
Test Case 2: Password Encryption Verification
Steps:
Create a new account.
Verify stored password in database.
Expected Result:
Password is encrypted and not stored as plain text.
9. Performance Testing
Test Case 1: Multiple User Load Test
Steps:
Simulate multiple users accessing the system simultaneously.
Perform trip searches and bookings.
Expected Result:
System responds within acceptable time.
No crashes occur.
10. Usability Testing
Test Case 1: Interface Navigation
Steps:
Navigate through all major pages.
Check menus, buttons, and forms.
Expected Result:
Navigation is simple and user-friendly.
All pages load correctly.
Conclusion

This QA Test Plan ensures that the Intercity Ride Sharing System is thoroughly tested for functionality, reliability, performance, and security. The testing process helps identify defects early, improve user experience, and ensure the system meets project requirements before deployment.

